    public static final String f15588f0 = "Build an HTML/Android WebView app that reads the device location.\nThe user wants: [DESCRIBE YOUR APP IDEA HERE].\nUse the global `AndroidAPI` JavaScript bridge.\nAvailable methods:\n- `AndroidAPI.requestPermission('android.permission.ACCESS_FINE_LOCATION', callbackId)`\n- `AndroidAPI.hasPermission('android.permission.ACCESS_FINE_LOCATION')`\n- `AndroidAPI.getLocation(callbackId)` — fires `locationResult` with `{callbackId, success, latitude, longitude, accuracy, provider, time, fromLastKnown, error}`.\n- `AndroidAPI.startLocationUpdates(callbackId)` / `AndroidAPI.stopLocationUpdates()` — fires `locationUpdate` per fix; the first one carries `status` such as `started:gps`.\n- `AndroidAPI.getAddress(latitude, longitude, callbackId)` — fires `addressResult` with `{callbackId, success, address, countryCode, error}` (reverse geocoding, no extra permission).\nListen with `window.onAndroidEvent = function(event, data) { if (event === 'locationResult') { ... } };` — an assigned handler, not a registration call.\n`error` is `permission_denied`, `provider_disabled`, `timeout` (no fix within 15s), `superseded` or `permission_revoked`; `fromLastKnown` marks a cached fix returned instantly.\nWrite clean, responsive HTML with inline CSS, a permission request button and a location display.\nReturn only the complete HTML file.";

    /* renamed from: g0, reason: collision with root package name */
    public static final String f15590g0 = "Build an HTML/Android WebView app that captures photos and shows a camera preview.\nThe user wants: [DESCRIBE YOUR APP IDEA HERE].\nUse the global `AndroidAPI` JavaScript bridge.\nResults come back as events. Register a listener with either form (they are both delivered):\n- `window.onAndroidEvent = function(event, data) { /* ... */ };`\n- `window.addEventListener('cameraResult', function(e) { var data = e.detail; });`\n`window.onAndroidEvent(...)` is NOT a registration call — never call it like `window.onAndroidEvent('cameraResult', cb)`.\nAvailable methods:\n- `AndroidAPI.requestPermission('android.permission.CAMERA', callbackId)`\n- `AndroidAPI.capturePhoto(callbackId)` — fires `cameraResult` with `{callbackId, success, base64, error}`; `base64` is a `data:image/jpeg;base64,...` URL, `error` is `permission_denied`, `cancelled`, `no_camera_app`, `capture_file_missing` or `encode_failed`.\n- `AndroidAPI.capturePhoto(callbackId, 'front')` — front camera through CameraX (needs CAMERA declared and granted); fires the same `cameraResult`, `error` may be `camera_permission_not_declared` or `front_capture_failed`.\n- `AndroidAPI.compressImage(base64Data, maxWidth, quality, callbackId)` — fires `imageCompressResult` with `{callbackId, success, base64, width, height, bytes, error}`; use it before uploading or storing a photo.\n- `AndroidAPI.startCameraPreview()` / `AndroidAPI.stopCameraPreview()` — native preview overlay; fires `cameraPreviewResult` with `{success, active, error}` (`error` may be `pro_required` or `permission_denied`).\nPlain HTML also works without the bridge: `<input type=\"file\" accept=\"image/*\" capture>` now offers the camera in the chooser.\nWrite clean, responsive HTML with inline CSS, capture and preview buttons, a status line and an image display area.\nReturn only the complete HTML file.";

    /* renamed from: h0, reason: collision with root package name */
    public static final String f15592h0 = "Build an HTML/Android WebView app that records audio from the microphone.\nThe user wants: [DESCRIBE YOUR APP IDEA HERE].\nUse the global `AndroidAPI` JavaScript bridge.\nAvailable methods:\n- `AndroidAPI.requestPermission('android.permission.RECORD_AUDIO', callbackId)`\n- `AndroidAPI.startAudioRecording(fileName)` — fires `audioRecordingStartResult` with `{fileName, success, warning, error}` (`error`: `permission_denied`, `start_failed`, `invalid_file_name`; `warning`: `previous_recording_discarded`).\n- `AndroidAPI.stopAudioRecording(callbackId)` — fires `audioRecordingResult` with `{callbackId, success, path, fileName, size, mimeType, error}` (`error`: `no_active_recording`, `stop_failed`, `empty_recording`).\n- `AndroidAPI.getAudioFileBase64(fileName, callbackId)` — fires `audioFileResult` with `{callbackId, fileName, success, base64, mimeType, size, error}` so the clip can be played back.\nListen with `window.onAndroidEvent = function(event, data) { ... };` (assigned handler, not a registration call).\nWrite clean, responsive HTML with inline CSS and a record/stop button.\nReturn only the complete HTML file.";

